# AN ARCH LINUX MICROVM RUNNING KDE PLASMA MOBILE ON WAYLAND, ON A virtio-gpu DISPLAY.
#
# THE DISPLAY DEVICE IS virtio-gpu OVER PCIe, so card0 carries both a Virtual-1 output and
# renderD128 - the pair KWin's DRM backend needs. See the long note in arch-rootfs.sh.
#
# THE CAPTURE IS THE SCANOUT, AND THAT IS WHAT MAKES THIS VARIANT POSSIBLE AT ALL.
#
# MEASURED, and it is the whole reason this image ships no easystream evidence: KWin
# implements NEITHER zwlr_screencopy NOR ext-image-copy-capture - `strings kwin_wayland` finds
# zero occurrences of either - so there is no Wayland capture protocol to read. The only other
# route is KDE's ScreenCast portal, and that stops one step short:
#
#	portal: SelectDevices has NO restore token - Start will ask for consent
#	portal: SelectDevices ok
#	portal: no Response for /org/freedesktop/portal/desktop/request/1_51/est1
#
# Everything up to the consent dialog works; the dialog itself needs a human click that a
# headless boot cannot give, and the permission store cannot be seeded before the first grant
# (Set and SetPermission both answer "Id easystream not found" - the id is CREATED by a grant).
#
# BOTH LIMITS ARE ABOUT READING THE COMPOSITOR, NOT ABOUT THE PIXELS. virtio-gpu drives a real
# framebuffer, so qemu's screendump photographs exactly what KWin scanned out. That is what this
# walkthrough measures.

walkthrough "plasma-mobile microvm - the phone shell on Wayland, captured from the scanout"
  resolution 1024x768
  recording_resolution 1024x768

  needs arch-vmlinuz arch-initramfs arch.qcow2
  disk arch.qcow2

  boot as a microvm from kernel "arch-vmlinuz" and initramfs "arch-initramfs" with "console=ttyS0 root=/dev/vda rw rootfstype=ext4" with a desktop with memory 1536, waiting up to 240s

  the console will say "login"
  the console will say "vmuser"

  # THE SESSION'S OWN MARKER, printed by the image right before it execs the session command.
  the console will say "ARCH-SESSION-STARTING: plasma-mobile"

  # THE PHONE SHELL STARTUP: kwin_wayland, plasmashell, plasma-keyboard, then the shell's own
  # first layout. It is slower than a bare compositor, so the settle is longer than the others'.
  wait 35s

  # THE PIXELS, FROM THE GUEST'S OWN SCANOUT.
  read the whole screen as "screen"

  step "the screen is not black"
    check == {name: screen_is_not_black, from: screen, mode: mean_between, rect: [0, 0, 1024, 768], rect_at: [1024, 768], range: [1, 255]}
  step "the screen is not one flat colour"
    check == {name: screen_has_content, from: screen, mode: spread_between, rect: [0, 0, 1024, 768], rect_at: [1024, 768], range: [1, 128]}

  stop the machine by killing it, waiting up to 60s
